# Line endings are normalised to LF IN THE REPOSITORY, for every text and data file.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. This repository was authored on Windows and its analysis is run on
# Linux, and the committed artifacts are compared byte-for-byte in places:
# `test_determinism.py` rebuilds analysis_long_v2.csv under two PYTHONHASHSEED values
# and requires an identical file (C10, C11); `test_artifact_provenance.py` asserts no
# committed artifact blends the two harnesses. Without this file, `git` would hand a
# Windows clone CRLF and a Linux clone LF for the same commit, so those comparisons
# would be testing the checkout platform as much as the code.
#
# The run manifests happen to be insulated — `items_file_sha` is computed from
# `Path.read_text()`, which normalises newlines on the way in — but that is a lucky
# property of one call site, not a policy, and it is not something the next person
# should have to discover before trusting a hash.
#
# The same reasoning is why `*.docx` is listed under Binary below. It was committed on
# 2026-08-16 without an entry and picked up `text=auto eol=lf` from the catch-all, which
# is safe only because git sniffs the NUL bytes in a zip container and declines to
# convert it. That is auto-detection doing the right thing by luck, not a declaration,
# and the whole point of this file is to not rely on that.

# Everything text-like: normalise on commit, check out LF everywhere.
*                text=auto eol=lf

# Data and source: never touched, never converted on checkout.
*.csv            text eol=lf
*.md             text eol=lf
*.py             text eol=lf
*.yaml           text eol=lf
*.yml            text eol=lf
*.json           text eol=lf
*.txt            text eol=lf
*.sh             text eol=lf
*.ini            text eol=lf
.gitignore       text eol=lf
.gitattributes   text eol=lf

# Binary — never convert, never diff as text.
*.png            binary
*.jpg            binary
*.pdf            binary
*.pptx           binary
*.docx           binary
*.safetensors    binary
*.bin            binary
*.gguf           binary

# CSVs are deliberately left as ordinary diffable text. An earlier draft of this file
# marked them `-diff`, to keep `git diff` tidy — which is exactly wrong here. Seeing
# what a refit changed in variance_ratio_v2.csv is how C15 was sized (R inflated
# 2.70x) and how C21 was caught. A quiet diff is a worse default than a long one.
